    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="1032" n="1018" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1018"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.932/16: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-04T21:00:00+07:00">May 4, 1944—9 p.m.
                                [<hi rendition="#italic">a.m.?</hi>]</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 4—7:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>772. Foreign Minister in response to my approach, as instructed by your 568,
                    April 27, 8 p.m., expressed view that it would be more convenient <pb
                        facs="1033" n="1019" xml:id="pg1019"/> to Chinese side if conversations on
                    commercial treaty could be held in Chungking. I told him this would be entirely
                    acceptable to us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
